# Timiva Tailwind Rules

## Purpose

These rules define how Cursor must write Tailwind CSS in the Timiva project.

## Core rules

Cursor must:

```text
1. Use Tailwind CSS as the main styling tool.
2. Keep HTML semantic.
3. Add Chinese comments for major sections.
4. Write RWD by component, not all desktop first and all mobile later.
5. Use @apply only for repeated semantic component patterns.
6. Avoid random one-off hard-coded visual values.
```

## Semantic HTML

Prefer:

```html
<header>
<nav>
<main>
<section>
<article>
<footer>
```

Use `div` only when it is a layout wrapper without stronger semantic meaning.

## Chinese comments

Major sections must include Chinese comments, such as:

```astro
<!-- Header｜桌機版主導覽 -->
<!-- Header｜手機版主導覽 -->
<!-- Tool｜桌機版工具主體 -->
<!-- Tool｜手機版工具主體 -->
<!-- Footer｜桌機版頁尾 -->
<!-- Footer｜手機版頁尾 -->
```

## RWD order

Correct:

```text
Header desktop
Header mobile

Tool desktop
Tool mobile

Footer desktop
Footer mobile
```

Incorrect:

```text
All desktop sections first
All mobile sections at the end
```

## Forbidden

Cursor must not use:

```text
inline style
!important
CSS id selector
random hard-coded colors
page-specific duplicate layout systems
```

IDs may be used for accessibility or JavaScript, but not as CSS selectors.
